    "sourceWikitext": "__NOTOC__\n{{recipesummary|category=Bread recipes|servings=12|time=1 hour|difficulty=2\n}}\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:North American cuisines|North America]] | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Ireland|Irish cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Breakfast|Breakfast cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Vegetarian cuisine|Vegetarian cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Bread|Bread]]\n\n== Ingredients ==\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:Whole Wheat|whole-wheat]]\n* 2 cups [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 2 cups [[Cookbook:Buttermilk|buttermilk]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to [[Cookbook:Oven_temperatures|325°F]] (165°C / gasmark 3).\n# Use [[Cookbook:Cooking Spray|cooking spray]] or grease and then lightly flour a 9x5x3-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] [[Cookbook:Cake Pan|baking pan]].\n# Combine flour, baking soda, and salt in a large mixing bowl.\n# Form a cavity in the middle.\n# Pour in the buttermilk.\n# Mix until just moistened. Too much mixing will make it tough.\n# Gently shape the [[Cookbook:Dough|dough]] to fit pan.\n# Cut the top at least three times with a knife.\n# [[Cookbook:Bake|Bake]] for 65–70 minutes, or until a toothpick inserted in the bread comes out clean.\n# Cool on a [[Cookbook:Cooling Rack|wire rack]].\n# Wrap in tea-towel or [[Cookbook:Aluminium Foil|foil]] several hours or overnight for best flavor.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n* If you're in a hurry, bake at 375°F for 35–40 minutes.\n* Buttermilk could be substituted with a tablespoon of [[Cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]] or [[Cookbook:Vinegar|vinegar]] in milk.\n* \"Baker's Secret\" is a brand of cooking spray that includes the flour.\n\n\n[[Category:Inexpensive recipes]]\n[[Category:Irish recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for bread]]\n[[Category:Breakfast recipes]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using buttermilk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cooking spray]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]",
